                <h2>Common Questions</h2>
<h3>1. Why Did Ads Stop When There Was Still Balance?</h3>
<p>This is one of the most frequent issues for marketing teams. The problem often lies not in the account balance itself, but in <strong>budget-level settings</strong>.</p>
<p>When you set daily budgets or lifetime budgets, ads pause once they hit that limit—even if there's still money in the account. For example, an e-commerce team had $2,000 remaining, but an ad set had a $50 daily budget. At 3 PM, the budget exhausted, ads paused, even though the account still had funds.</p>
<p><strong>Key principle</strong>: Don't just check total account balance—monitor campaign/ad set budget consumption status.</p>
<h3>2. What Balance Threshold Should You Set for Alerts?</h3>
<p>There's no universal answer—it depends on your deposit processing time.</p>
<p>Different payment methods have vastly different processing speeds: PayPal/credit cards are usually instant, while bank transfers take 1-3 business days, potentially longer during holidays. Based on Yoyi Media's operational experience: <strong>alert thresholds should cover deposit processing time plus buffer time</strong>.</p>
<ul>
<li>Teams relying on bank transfers: Set alerts at 7 days' spend</li>
<li>Teams with instant payment methods: Set alerts at 3 days' spend</li>
<li>New accounts or unstable periods: Raise thresholds appropriately</li>
</ul>
<h3>3. Should You Enable Auto-Top-Up?</h3>
<p><strong>Yes, but with a backup system</strong>.</p>
<p>One utility app team encountered this: auto-top-up was enabled, but the linked credit card had insufficient limit. The top-up failed, balance hit zero, and they didn't discover it for 3 hours. This proves auto-top-up isn't foolproof.</p>
<p>Recommended approach: Enable auto-top-up as the first layer of protection, while establishing a manual review mechanism. When balance drops below a certain threshold, someone must confirm the deposit status.</p>
<h3>4. How to Manage Balance Alerts Across Multiple Accounts?</h3>
<p>Manual tracking is inefficient and error-prone.</p>
<p>When managing 5+ ad accounts, professional tools for unified monitoring are recommended. Yoyi Media's multi-account balance alert system provides:</p>
<ul>
<li>Real-time sync across all platform accounts</li>
<li>Customizable alert rules (different thresholds for different accounts)</li>
<li>Multi-channel notifications (WeChat/email/SMS)</li>
<li>Automatic archival of deposit records for reconciliation</li>
</ul>
<p>A gaming team previously used Excel manual tracking and discovered account depletion at 3 AM. After integrating the system, alerts trigger when balance falls below 2 days' spend, allowing operations staff to confirm normal status before bed.</p>
<h3>5. What to Do When Deposits Are Delayed?</h3>
<p>During deposit delays, <strong>the priority is protecting core campaigns</strong>.</p>
<p>Specific steps:<br />
1. Immediately check deposit status—confirm whether it's a processing delay or account issue<br />
2. Pause non-core campaigns or reduce budgets to extend account runway<br />
3. Contact platform account managers or agents for emergency deposit channels<br />
4. If backup accounts exist, migrate or activate core campaigns there</p>
<p><strong>Decision framework</strong>: If balance can sustain for more than 1 hour, focus on resolving the deposit. If less than 1 hour, prioritize pausing activities to preserve the account.</p>
<h2>Alert Setup Checklist</h2>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Do you know average daily spend for each account?</li>
<li>[ ] Have you tested actual deposit processing times? (Different channels vary significantly)</li>
<li>[ ] Have you distinguished between account balance and campaign budgets?</li>
<li>[ ] Are alert notifications sent to channels the responsible person actually monitors?</li>
<li>[ ] Does auto-top-up have a backup verification mechanism?</li>
<li>[ ] Do you have a unified monitoring dashboard for multiple accounts?</li>
</ul>
<h2>Conclusion</h2>
<p>Balance alerting isn't simply "setting a reminder"—it requires understanding account consumption patterns, deposit channel timelines, and multi-layer budget logic. Establishing a robust balance management system saves not only ad spend but also the opportunity cost of missing breakout campaign moments.</p>
